.TH ACTIVITYTRACK-TUI 1 "November 2026" "activitytrack-tui 0.9.4-beta2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
activitytrack-tui \- ActivityTrack in the terminal, full screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B activitytrack-tui
.RB [ \-\-data
.IR folder ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B activitytrack-tui
shows the activities running and the Home list of ActivityTrack (to-dos and
stopped activities) full screen, and works them from the keyboard. It is the
same application as the desktop tray application and the command line
.BR activitytrack (1),
on the same data and pairing: what they do shows within a second. The sync
runs in the background, every 30 seconds and after each change. To pair the
PC use the desktop application or
.BR "activitytrack pair" .
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR "\(ua \(da" ", " j " " k
Move the selection.
.TP
.B Enter
The actions of the selected row: the commands of an activity, completing
it, starting, finishing, postponing or ignoring a to-do.
.TP
.B n
A new activity: description, client (typing filters the list; a new name
becomes a new client when the policy allows it), work or travel, start time.
.TP
.B t
A new to-do.
.TP
.BR p ", " s ", " v ", " u
Pause or resume, stop, travel, suspend the selected activity (or the one
running).
.TP
.B d
The selected to-do is done.
.TP
.BR f ", " g
The period and the states of the list.
.TP
.B r
Sync now.
.TP
.BR q ", " Esc
Quit; in a popup, close it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-data " folder"
Another data folder than the shared one.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/activitytrack/
The data shared with the desktop application and the command line.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR activitytrack (1)
.SH AUTHOR
The ActivityTrack contributors, https://github.com/zipclaude/activitytrack-tui
